Open the laptop

Connect buttons to laptop
Open Arduino ide
the DiscoverDay.ino code should automatically pop up
click the checkmark
click the arrow to the right
if there are any problems go to tools and make sure the board selected says arduino mega or mega 2560
also take note of which port it is connected to (COM4)....
can close it out. 

open visual studio code. 
DiscoverDay.py should automatically pop up....
make sure the right com is listed as the serial port (line 17)

connect the glasses to the samsung phone
open the phone
turn on the mobile hot spot
go back to the laptop and connect to the phone's hotspot
now on the phone, open the neon companion app
check the ip address and make sure it matches what is typed into line 56 in the python code

when ready, click the play button in top right corner of teh python code
it may take a minute or two but you shoul dsee that Arduino is connected and that the phone is connected
when you click start, the beep will play, a button will light up, and neon glasses begin recording.
the beeps and buttons will cycle through and teh recording is continued.
when you click stop, recording is stopped. when you exit, saved to an excel fiel which is saved in eth downloads folder
if you open file explorer and go to dowbloads, it will be teh first thing there

when finished, dont forget to disconnect teh hotspot so you dont waste data. 
